      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings: Revenues exceed analysts expectations while EPS lags behind",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹38.59 (up from ₹24.01 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹41.6b (up 26% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹1.56b (up 60% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 3.7% (up from 2.9% in 3Q 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 4.1%. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 12%. Revenue is forecast to grow 9.9% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 10% growth forecast for the Auto Components industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 20% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 33% per year, which means it is tracking significantly ahead of earnings growth.",
